# rpm — real-world examples

## Install / remove packages

```sh
# Install with progress hashes
rpm -ivh <rpm>

# Upgrade (installs if not present)
rpm -Uvh <rpm>

# Remove a package
rpm -e <package>
```

## Query packages and files

```sh
# What package owns this file?
rpm -qf /path/to/file

# What files does an installed package provide?
rpm -ql <package>

# What files are inside an .rpm file (not yet installed)?
rpm -qpl <rpm>

# What requires this package or file?
rpm -q --whatrequires <package>
rpm -q --whatrequires <file>

# List all installed packages
rpm -qa
```

## Verify / rebuild the rpm database

```sh
cd /var/lib/rpm/
/usr/lib/rpm/rpmdb_verify Packages
mv Packages Packages.bad
/usr/lib/rpm/rpmdb_dump Packages.bad | /usr/lib/rpm/rpmdb_load Packages
/usr/lib/rpm/rpmdb_verify Packages
rpm -qa > /dev/null
rpm -vv --rebuilddb
```

## Yum interaction (RHEL/CentOS)

```sh
# Edit /etc/yum.conf to remove an exclusion (e.g. for httpd)
vim /etc/yum.conf
```

## Homelab examples (OpenSUSE Tumbleweed)

```sh
# Verify a package's files haven't been tampered with
rpm -V openssh

# Which package owns zypper itself?
rpm -qf $(which zypper)

# 20 most recently installed packages (handy after a `zypper dup`)
rpm -qa --last | head -20

# Read a package's changelog
rpm -q --changelog kernel-default | head -30

# Prefer zypper for dependency-resolved installs on Tumbleweed:
sudo zypper install <package>
```

## Flag reference

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-i` / `-U` | Install / upgrade |
| `-v` `-h` | Verbose + hash progress bar |
| `-e` | Erase (remove) |
| `-q` | Query mode |
| `-a` | All installed packages |
| `-f <file>` | Owner of file |
| `-l` | List files |
| `-p <rpm>` | Query an .rpm file instead of the DB |
| `-V` | Verify files against the DB |
